:::oak-heading {id="title" level="1"}
Subordination with ‘because’
:::

:::oak-task {id="task-a"}

:::oak-heading {id="task-a-heading" level="2"}
Task A: Understanding dependency
:::

:::oak-instruction {id="task-a-instruction" keep-with-next="true"}
Circle the stretched second idea that is dependent on the first idea in each sentence. Remember that it will begin with ‘because’.
:::

:::oak-question {id="question-1"}
:::oak-paragraph {id="sentence-1"}
The gong on the clock sounded because it was midnight.
:::

:::oak-paragraph {id="sentence-2"}
We can’t go outside because you haven’t got your shoes on.
:::

:::oak-paragraph {id="sentence-3"}
I enjoy going to school because we learn interesting things.
:::

:::oak-paragraph {id="sentence-4"}
Aisha put her hand up because she knew the answer.
:::
:::
:::

:::oak-task {id="task-b"}

:::oak-heading {id="task-b-heading" level="2"}
Task B: Stretching with ‘because’
:::

:::oak-instruction {id="task-b-instruction" keep-with-next="true"}
Read these first ideas. Pick one and use ‘because’ to stretch the first idea with a reason.
:::

:::oak-question {id="question-2"}
:::oak-paragraph {id="first-idea-1"}
The little girl cried
:::

:::oak-paragraph {id="first-idea-2"}
Sam felt exhausted
:::

:::oak-paragraph {id="first-idea-3"}
The dog barked loudly
:::

